 This is mainly useful for debugging provider serialization and cache behavior.
 
+#### provider_request
+
+Fires after all `before_provider_request` transforms and before the provider sends
+the request. Use it to capture the final provider payload. Each handler receives
+its own structured clone; mutations and return values cannot change the transport
+payload or another observer's snapshot. The event's `model` is the request's
+`{ provider, id }`, independent of later session/model changes.
+
+```typescript
+pi.on("provider_request", (event, ctx) => {
+  // event.payload - final provider payload snapshot
+  // event.model - request-time model identity
+});
+```
+
+This event requires the provider to call `options.onPayload`, like the transform
+hook. Errors in observers are reported as extension errors and leave the request
+unchanged.
+
 #### after_provider_response
 
